Shafaq News- Baghdad Iraqi lawmaker and former Communications Minister Hiyam al-Yasiri has questioned the appointment of four deputy prime ministers in the government of Ali al-Zaidi, asking about th
Political forces had divided up the positions and agreed to vote on them next Thursday, she said, adding that &ldquo;Appointing four deputy prime ministers violates Article 139 of the Iraqi Constitution.&rdquo;
Addressing members of parliament, al-Yasiri urged them not to base their votes solely on the positions of political party and bloc leaders, reminding them &ldquo;of their responsibility for their decisions.&rdquo;
Al-Yasiri sarcastically suggested that citizens be allowed to volunteer for the positions if they carry no salaries.
According to the parliament&rsquo;s media office, the parliament will meet Thursday to vote on candidates for vacant and newly created cabinet positions, including deputy prime minister posts.

Shafaq News- Erbil Iraq will bring armed factions&rsquo; weapons under state control and prevent activities outside state authority by June 30, 2027, Sabah al-Numan, spokesman for the commander-in-ch
Speaking at a panel during the Middle East Research Institute (MERI) Forum 2026 in Erbil, titled &ldquo;After the Global Coalition: Iraq, the Kurdistan Region and the New Regional Balance,&rdquo; al-Numan added that the withdrawal of the US-led Coalition &ldquo;had removed all pretexts for refusing to place weapons under state control and unify security decision-making.&rdquo;
He said that armed factions had pledged to honor a &ldquo;goodwill initiative&rdquo; and comply with a 90-day deadline announced by the government to halt any activities targeting a neighboring country. &ldquo;All of Iraq&rsquo;s borders are now fully secured, and no entity operating outside the law can threaten a neighboring country.&rdquo;
